       Ensure all three crop signatures (including bg cells within bbox) are unique.
    3. Duplicate sprite A to get 2 copies; duplicate sprite B to get 2 copies;
       keep sprite C as the singleton (5 sprites total).
    4. Place all 5 sprites on the grid so no two bounding boxes overlap
       and each is at least 1 cell from any other bbox.
       Allow touching grid border.
    5. Output is the crop of sprite C.
